{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"862335a95925ff8add325fc95a77bc20247cdea2acd3ab917b42d6aac84b2cf9","digest":{"component_or_area":"tickets store (git-backed)","key_entities":["rebar._commands.compact_trigger.maybe_compact","compact_txn._compact_locked","rebar._store.sync._union_merge","*/.archived","*/.write.lock","rebar fsck","rebar doctor","rebar compact-all","--include-archived","INTENT JOURNAL","SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT","compact.trigger","tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py"],"problem_keywords":["wedge","crash-atomic","compaction","sync recovery","git merge abort","tracked markers","dirty tree","fsck","doctor repair","data loss"],"propositions":["Parallel multi-session compaction writes corrupt the worktree (snapshot writes, retire renames, archive deletions) before git commit, leaving untracked and tracked artifacts that block future syncs and create P0 data-loss risk when merge aborts strand local commits.","Tracked runtime markers (*/.archived, */.write.lock) committed before gitignore patterns exist are never un-tracked, causing marker churn to perpetually appear as dirty tree in git status.","Store-wide scans (fsck, compact-all) lack active-only default scoping, incurring cost proportional to total archived tickets rather than active working set.","Crash-interrupted compaction folds lack atomic rollback and recovery, leaving partial mutations (renamed sources, uncommitted snapshots) stranded in the worktree indefinitely."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787495658190857001,"uuid":"b93335c9-7122-419a-af13-0959141ffa75"}